NOTES_HTML='''<p>Michelin: the 2026 California selection, announced June 24, 2026 in San Diego. Californios in the Mission was promoted to three stars — the first Mexican restaurant in the world to hold them — joining Atelier Crenn, Benu and Quince in the city; Enclos in Sonoma also reached three, giving the Bay Area and Wine Country six three-star restaurants with the French Laundry and SingleThread. Restaurant Naides and Wolfsbane earned first stars in the city, Troubadour Bread &amp; Bistro in Healdsburg; Kitchen Istanbul and Joodooboo joined the Bib list; Good Good Culture Club and Ippuku returned to it. California now counts 83 stars and 117 Bib Gourmands. The Progress, Kin Khao and Anchor Brewing are flagged because each changed shape since the last edition.</p><p>Bars: True Laurel (№17) and Pacific Cocktail Haven (№16) held 2025 North America's 50 Best rankings; their 2026 placings weren't confirmed for this edition.</p><p>Occasion chips for San Francisco are editorial assignments, by category and price. Tock and Resy split the counters; the Amex credit works at both.</p><p>Photography via Pexels (royalty-free): three photographs, cropped and reused across the twelve sections.</p>'''
